    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this two-bedroom end-of-terrace property to the market on the ever-popular Lough Conn Road. Crucially, this property qualifies for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, offering fantastic financial assistance to prospective purchasers looking to renovate.\n\nThe location is ideal for growing families and commuters alike. Lough Conn Road is exceptionally well-positioned directly adjacent to a selection of reputable primary and secondary schools, making the morning school run completely effortless. Ballyfermot Village is within easy walking distance, offering a wide array of local shops, supermarkets, cafes, and sports amenities. Excellent public transport options, including frequent bus routes into Dublin City Centre, are close at hand, while the M50 motorway, Naas Road, and Liffey Valley Shopping Centre are all just a short drive away.\n\nBright internal living accommodation offers a practical layout with immense potential to customize or extend (subject to relevant planning permission). Downstairs comprises an entrance hallway leading into a spacious living area and kitchen space. Upstairs, there are two generous double bedrooms and a main family bathroom. Externally, the property boasts a side entrance that leads to a substantial, private rear garden offering endless potential for outdoor entertaining, landscaping, or future expansion.\n\nWith its prime positioning, proximity to local schools, large plot, and eligibility for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, 120 Lough Conn Road is an opportunity not to be missed. \n\nViewing is highly advised. Call RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS today for further information or to arrange a viewing!\n\nAdditional Features;\n•BER G\n•C. 60 sq m\n•2 BED / 1 BATH\n•End-of-terrace property with side entrance\n•Qualifies for the vacant property refurbishment grant\n•Fantastic renovation project tremendous potential to modernise\n•Generous private rear garden offering room to extend (SPP)\n•Two spacious double bedrooms upstairs\n•Unbeatable location directly convenient to multiple primary & secondary schools\n•Short stroll to Ballyfermot Village and local amenities\n•Off street parking\n•Excellent public transport links to Dublin City Centre\n•Easy access to M50 motorway and Liffey Valley SC\n•Ideal for First-Time Buyers, Families, and Investors\n\nDirections\nFrom Ballyfermot Road heading outbound towards Cherry Orchard, turn right onto Kylemore Road and take an immediate left onto Blackditch Road. Continue straight along Blackditch Road, then take a right turn onto Lough Conn Road. Proceed straight down the road, and No. 120 will be located on your right-hand side, clearly identified by our Ray Cooke Auctioneers 'For Sale' sign.\n"
      },
